        "S4.E11",
        "A3.Ex160"
      ],
      "statement": "For Λ=diag(λ₁,…,λ_d), det Λ=∏_{i=1}^{d}λ_i.",
      "reason_for_phase2_addition": "The source uses det Λ; the sealed type makes its diagonal product explicit. Phase 1 had not split out this identity. It is a genuine required proof/representation bridge, not an additional theorem premise.",
      "source_proof_detail": "Standard finite-dimensional determinant identity, implicit in the source diagonal-matrix definition; not separately stated or proved in C.4.",
      "proof_status": "UNPROVED_IN_THIS_REVIEW",
      "compiled_dependency": null
    },
    {
      "id": "semantic-adapter:arxiv2610.20492v1:source-i-to-Fin-d",
      "kind": "source-to-type-index-adapter",
      "source_status": "SEMANTIC_EXPANSION",
      "source_anchors": [
        "S4.E11"
      ],
      "statement": "For j:Fin d, source index i=j.val+1 runs exactly through 1,…,d. Then i−1/2=j.val+1/2, and the two θ, λ formulae agree after this reindexing.",
      "proof_status": "SEMANTIC_COMPARISON_ONLY_NOT_A_LEAN_PROOF",
      "division_sense": "The sealed θ has type Fin d→ℝ. Its half, the dimension cast, multiplication by π and division by d are real operations; d≥2 ensures a positive nonzero denominator."
    },
    {
      "id": "sealed-statement:sha256:1c55aaf1c9c11d4e1cdb1b565d3327fa8274e9a78f6440ca577b6c49b880f2dd",
      "kind": "sealed-type-endpoint",
      "source_status": "MATCHES_SELECTED_COMPONENT_SUBJECT_TO_DISTINCT_TOPOLOGY_CHALLENGE",
      "seal_file": "research-wiki/paper-contributions/GaussianComplexity/fixed-spectrum-determinant-statement-seal.json",
      "seal_sha256": "15d7e92a84617b97ee7e9b105da967e1c6598a9ca2d6a06596c8974e25b05354",
      "signature_sha256": "1c55aaf1c9c11d4e1cdb1b565d3327fa8274e9a78f6440ca577b6c49b880f2dd",
      "exact_signature_utf8": "theorem actual_precision_det {d : ℕ} (hd : 2 ≤ d)\n    {κ : ℝ} (hκ : 2 ≤ κ)\n    (O : Matrix.orthogonalGroup (Fin d) ℝ) :\n    let θ : Fin d → ℝ := fun i => ((i.val : ℝ) + 1 / 2) * Real.pi / (d : ℝ)\n    let diagonalValue : Fin d → ℝ := fun i =>\n      (κ + 1) / 2 + (κ - 1) / 2 * Real.cos (θ i)\n    let A : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ :=\n      (O : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ) * Matrix.diagonal diagonalValue *\n        (O : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℝ).transpose\n    A.det = ∏ i : Fin d, diagonalValue i\n",
      "claim_boundary": "Actual precision determinant equals the explicit product of the literal grid values, pointwise for every full real orthogonal O. No integral, density, Z, probability or lower-bound claim.",
      "proof_status": "NOT_INSPECTED_NOT_PROVED_BY_THIS_REVIEW"
    }
  ],
